{"seq":1270,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"1270.json: “Residents will save $15 a month because of the growth, an amount negotiated up from $8.” B links it to v4, v5 and v16.","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and §5.3: evidence must help answer the question; unrelated details are not kept.","mechanism":"B files a local electricity-customer benefit under questions about four hyperscalers’ spending and compute capacity without a connection to those outcomes."}
{"seq":1270,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"1270.json: “The amount of money paid and the amount of relief given to residents will remain unchanged should the project be delayed or canceled.” Also: “OpenAI will be charged with the cost of installing the power grid it will use to operate.” Both are linked to v4, v5 and v16.","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and §5.3; D259: an indirect link must make the answer to the question more or less likely.","mechanism":"B files contract terms about OpenAI and local electricity customers under the four named hyperscalers’ spending and capacity questions without showing how the terms affect those questions."}
{"seq":1270,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"1270.json: “The deal commits OpenAI to 3.1 gigawatts, about 14% of Georgia Power’s total capacity” is linked to v4, v5 and v16; the approval of the same OpenAI contract is also linked to v60.","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and D250 boundary 2: another party’s information needs a discernible path to the question it is filed under.","mechanism":"The output treats an OpenAI power commitment as evidence for spending, spending growth and compute capacity of other companies; the article does not establish their participation or quantify an effect on them."}
{"seq":1271,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1271.json: A and B both quote “the headline PCE price index rose to 3.7% year-on-year in July”; _ledger.json stores the same reading as e4423 for v86 and e4425 for v77.","rule":"Signed standard §2: one statement in one article is one evidence record, which may link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A and B independently return the same reading, and split_seven_day_poc.py build_handover appends their evidence separately without reconciling the shared statement."}
{"seq":1271,"lane":"judging","class":"unsupported-precision","severity":"serious","evidence":"1271.json v86: “About 3.4% year over year in December 2026: carrying forward July's 0.2% month-on-month increase implies a roughly 2.4% annualized monthly pace ... the evidence does not provide the prior-year monthly comparison needed for a precise calculation.”","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 and §7: preserve the limits of evidence and support the conclusion it is used for.","mechanism":"The judgement selects a specific December year-over-year rate and outcome from one monthly change, although it acknowledges that the prior-year comparisons needed for the calculation are missing."}
{"seq":1273,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"inverted-revenue-ladder","severity":"blocker","evidence":"1273.json v87: “Strongly bullish: FY2026 AI-related semiconductor revenue is below $18 billion” and “Strongly bearish: FY2026 AI-related semiconductor revenue is at least $24 billion.”","rule":"split_seven_day_poc.py META_SYSTEM requires a company outcome’s labels to mean good or bad for the business; signed standard §4 requires meaningful outcomes.","mechanism":"Record preparation reverses the business meaning of the revenue ranges. The ladder and numeric-bound checks accept the ordered labels and partition without detecting that inversion."}
{"seq":1273,"lane":"judging","class":"lower-bound-treated-as-point","severity":"serious","evidence":"1273.json v87: the source says revenue “could exceed $20 billion”; the judgement says the evidence supports “an outcome just over the guidance threshold” and chooses $20 billion to below $22 billion.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 and §7: preserve the limits of a statement and support the conclusion drawn from it.","mechanism":"The judgement turns an open-ended forecast into a bounded outcome without evidence establishing that revenue is more likely to remain below $22 billion."}
{"seq":1275,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1275.json: A and B both quote “2026 capex $60–$64B”; _ledger.json stores e4432 under v88 and e4436 under v79.","rule":"Signed standard §2: one statement in one article is one evidence record, which may link to relevant questions; D259 permits the same answer’s own candidate alongside an existing question.","mechanism":"A and B use the same prior library and their outputs are appended independently, so the writer receives two records for the same statement."}
{"seq":1275,"lane":"B","class":"weak-future-period-link","severity":"serious","evidence":"1275.json: “6nm Xring O100 NPU for on-device LLMs (planned next year), and 3nm Xring D100 for AVs (planned next year)” is filed under v79, TSMC’s FY2026 total-revenue question; B notes that the article “does not specify orders or revenue for these planned chips.”","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and D259: a driver must make the linked outcome more or less likely; D250 boundary 2 requires a discernible path for another company’s activity.","mechanism":"B links a customer’s next-year product plans to the current-year revenue question without identifying a current-year order, shipment or revenue effect."}
{"seq":1275,"lane":"matching","class":"unsupported-repeat","severity":"serious","evidence":"1275.json marks “Q2 sales +$40.2B” as repeat of e4310. B dates that statement “Q2 2025”; _ledger.json e4310 reports “Q2 2026” revenue of NT$1.2 trillion.","rule":"D202 and D204: a repeat is a matching opinion about the same statement, while both source records remain stored; signed standard §5.4 preserves period and quantity.","mechanism":"Jev labels the two statements same_statement at 0.77 despite the periods recorded in the trace differing. The article’s period is ambiguous, so the available text does not establish that they are the same statement."}
{"seq":1275,"lane":"judging","class":"guidance-boundary-mismatch","severity":"minor","evidence":"1275.json v88: the judgement says “TSMC’s FY2026 guidance is $60–$64 billion, which is rung 3”; rung 3 is “at least $60,000,000,000 and below $64,000,000,000,” while rung 4 starts at $64 billion.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4 preserves the source’s limits; META_SYSTEM requires each numeric upper bound to be exclusive.","mechanism":"The judgement treats the entire stated guidance range as belonging to rung 3 even though its $64 billion endpoint falls in rung 4."}
{"summary":{"items_read":[1269,1270,1271,1272,1273,1274,1275,1276],"classes":{"unhelpful-evidence":3,"same-article-evidence-duplicated":2,"unsupported-precision":1,"inverted-revenue-ladder":1,"lower-bound-treated-as-point":1,"weak-future-period-link":1,"unsupported-repeat":1,"guidance-boundary-mismatch":1}}}